  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRO-RIGHTS: Promoting the Rights of Venezuelan Refugees and Migrants in Latin America and the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute to enhancing protection for refugees and migrants in Colombia, Peru, and other LAC countries, particularly among Venezuelan women and girls. In Colombia, IOM will strengthen prevention and response to sexual exploitation of children and adolescents, within the framework of Commercial Sexual Exploitation of Children (CSEC) in both virtual and trafficking in persons contexts. In Peru, IOM will improve access to regularization among Venezuelan refugees and migrants, particularly women and girls &#x2013; ultimately contributing to their integration and protection. To achieve this, the initiative aims at the following outcomes: Increased awareness and access by children and adolescents, particularly girls, to initiatives and services that prevent sexual exploitation in project locations; increased effectiveness of Sexual Exploitation response routes and protocols, particularly for girls and adolescent girls; Venezuelan refugees and migrants, particularly women and girls, are informed and supported in accessing regularization and protection services; strengthened government institutions improve provision of gender-sensitive regularization and documentation services for Venezuelan refugees and migrants, particularly women and girls, strengthened regional capacities to respond to trafficking of Venezuelan refugees and migrants, particularly women and girls in LAC.</narrative>
  </description>
